From d9676f812b06ab69049678a4a5dcf416190863a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:31:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sim): the hidden-rest scan answers past its holding
 budget

Past the 1.2 M-cell / 40 M-claim budgets the hidden-rest scan read
RestUnjudged (NOT JUDGED) and blocked the post. Those numbers now
bound what the scan holds at once: a lattice that does not fit is
counted row by row, cut into row bands that do, and judged band by
band through the same body, so the verdict is the whole-lattice
verdict bit for bit. A new `work` budget (1 G visits + distances)
bounds the whole walk; past it, or when one row alone cannot be held,
the scan still says NOT JUDGED by name. The nearest ball-center query
goes through an exact uniform XY grid (scan_near), ring walk bounded
by XY ring distance and the path's Z gap.

Reading: a 21-plate stack, 1.07 M columns, 44.0 M claims (past the
shipped 40 M): was NOT JUDGED, now judged 41.206 mm hidden rest;
release 14.5 s (2.2 s without the hidden half).

Fixes #24

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
